<p class="small">Checked November 15, 2026, 02:14 UTC. All six repairs are now merged upstream. Sign-in code #230 passed exact-head CI and fresh review before its maintainer merged it; the store now adopts current upstream source through a one-way downstream merge, preserving both Account proof paths and the merchant theme. Public Before/After proof remains in each PR; source verification is not a release or shared-service deployment.</p>
<p class="small" data-feed-landings-review>Feed landings · <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/244">Template PR #244</a> · <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/tree/fix/feed-variant-urls">fork 06b0be5</a> supplies optional selected-member URLs without changing family canonicals or Commerce facts. Compiled main/head output with the same public catalog and proposed Commerce282 consumer checks all six size destinations; the current pinned XML/CSV and agent JSON remain identical. All568 units,101 workflows, typecheck, Registry size/site checks and24 built-Worker native landing checks pass; the dev-server seed refusal is disclosed separately. Ten own PRs are now open; this head’s complete desktop, phone, Registry, Playground and aggregate CI passes, with review requested afterward. Merchant adoption retains its own item query, not the generic variant query.</p>
<p class="small" data-cart-regression-review>Prepared regression inventory · <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/commit/3d1b690">off-live preparation 3d1b690</a> now passes all 1,235 units, 120 workflows with two optional skips, ten presentation cases, feature audit and full546-file typecheck on pinned Node24.22.0. Remaining legacy assertions are aligned with native checkout; correct beta artifacts, an ordinary source checkout and the exact Node pin resolve the local fixture failures without weakening checks. A hidden-summary fault fails its rendered test, then the component is restored unchanged; this supersedes the incomplete unit/workflow inventory below, not browser, signed migration or hosted-purchase qualifications. All nine authored upstream PRs remain open; no new source or review request was sent upstream.</p>
<p class="small" data-native-presentation-review>Native component coverage · <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/commit/1f5bbd0">off-live preparation 1f5bbd0</a> replaces the two obsolete journey assertions noted below with nine actual Astro-container renders, retaining source-level CSS/route boundaries. Named shipping/billing controls, autocomplete/countries, postal error association, safe retained values, digital/frozen forms and paid/non-paid print guidance pass; deliberate faults produce two field failures and four non-paid failures before byte-for-byte source restoration. Nine rendered cases,38 focused units and full546-file typecheck pass with no EmDash integration or permitted fetches; an all-unit baseline timed out without a complete report, so this is not a full-suite or installed-backend/browser/provider qualification. No runtime is changed; all nine upstream PRs remain open without new review or failing checks at19:16UTC.</p>
<p class="small" data-merchant-cart-queue-review>Merchant queue preparation · <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/commit/1e24719">off-live Field Journal 1e24719</a> provisionally carries the PR243 policy, preserving merchant controls and accessible cart-link counts. Nine actual Registry-installed beta2 browser contexts cover queued changes and captured native fallback in explicitly asserted Light/Dark at390/1440, plus plain forms; four painted audits,49 focused units,36 shopper safeguards and full544-file typecheck pass. <a href="/pr-proof/merchant-cart-queue/after-1440-light.png">Light desktop</a> / <a href="/pr-proof/merchant-cart-queue/after-390-dark.png">Dark phone</a> retain public-only fixture facts; the real eight-write budget remains enabled and two inherited legacy markup assertions remain unresolved. No production runtime adoption, signed in-place upgrade or hosted purchase is claimed; all nine own PRs remain open with no new review or failed check at18:36UTC.</p>
<p class="small" data-server-cart-concurrency-report>Proposed repair · <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/issues/242">Template #242</a> / <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/243">PR #243</a> · <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/tree/fix/server-cart-change-queue">fork d0a950a</a> captures and queues Change/Remove forms, replacing the attached section so both successful changes remain visible. <a href="/pr-proof/template-store-cart-queue/before-1440.png">Unchanged main</a> / <a href="/pr-proof/template-store-cart-queue/after-1440.png">proposed fix</a> show the actual installed-beta result, not a reload workaround; desktop/phone regressions, 567 units, 101 workflow checks, typecheck, Registry compilation and four painted audits pass locally. Exact-head desktop, phone, Registry, Playground and aggregate CI passed at 18:07 UTC; review was requested afterward. Only reporting ships live, and no checkout, order or hosted-service mutation occurred.</p>
<p class="small" data-picker-accessibility-review>Product option accessibility · <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/241">Template PR #241</a> · <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/tree/fix/variant-stock-status">fork 1b2d228</a> gives changing variant stock a retained polite/atomic status and native picker focus, with 44px option/mobile quantity targets and default dark action contrast raised from 4.43 to 4.54:1. Actual starter Before/After desktop Light and phone Dark images accompany main-fail/head-pass regressions; 569 units, 101 workflow checks, typecheck, Registry site build and four clean painted audits pass. The full local browser matrix stops at the same unchanged-main admin welcome/heap failure; exact-head desktop, phone, Registry and Playground CI all passed by November 16 at 11:07 UTC. A fresh review was requested after completion; review remains open. Backroad Bum already uses the matching status semantics and larger merchant controls; no signed plugin, payment, order or shared service changes.</p>
<p class="small" data-server-cart-stage>Server-cart dogfood · proposed <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/240">Template #240</a> at 2b780af with Commerce beta2 b460433 now passes isolated old-purchase recovery, 53 built-Worker HTTP cases and four desktop/phone plain/enhanced cart contexts. This tests the maintainers’ implementation, not a new Backroad Bum PR. Synthetic local Payments and disposable storage prove neither signed installation nor hosted checkout; the standard dev-server lane failed at fixture setup. The Field Journal branch now also qualifies an explicit earlier-checkout handoff against actual old-kernel disposable purchases; original live browsers and the signed upgrade remain unqualified, and the live stable plugin stays unchanged.</p>
<p class="small" data-installed-storefront-review>Registry-installed storefront · The whole prepared Field Journal source now runs with an actual EmDash-installed beta2 and no source sandbox mount; active Registry state and the downloaded backend digest are independently recorded. Plain/enhanced HTTPS forms preserve the $18 mug, saved quantities, Secure/HttpOnly cookies, invalid-edit intent and browser/origin isolation; eight painted cart/checkout Light/Dark audits are clean. <a href="/pr-proof/installed-storefront/cart-desktop-light.jpg">Desktop cart</a> / <a href="/pr-proof/installed-storefront/checkout-mobile-dark.jpg">phone checkout</a> show public-only fixture data: no Orders, hosted consents or Payments are copied or created, so checkout correctly stays unavailable. This closes the installed-artifact whole-storefront gap, not same-ID upgrade, production proxy configuration, full regression or hosted payment; only reporting ships on stable 0.8.0.</p>
<p class="small" data-registry-install-review>Actual Registry installation · EmDash1.4.0 verifies beta2 provenance and installs the published artifact after native permission consent, returning HTTP201 and active Registry state in a disposable store. The 130929-byte backend hash exactly matches the earlier source build; thirteen native HTTP checks qualify seven families/eleven members, $18 mug/$14 bandana, backorders/sold-out size, stale and invalid edits, separate capabilities and unavailable unconnected checkout, followed by a passing saved-cart read after process restart. <a href="/pr-proof/commerce-beta-registry/verified-consent.jpg">Verified consent</a> / <a href="/pr-proof/commerce-beta-registry/installed.jpg">installed release</a> show the synthetic development admin, with only catalog rows copied into the beta namespace and no Orders, hosted consents or Payments. This closes fresh signed-beta installation—not stable in-place upgrade, production configuration, full regression or hosted purchase; all seven own PRs await review and the live stable plugin remains 0.8.0.</p>
<p class="small" data-storefront-https-review>Merchant HTTPS rehearsal · <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/commit/7465e73">preparation 7465e73</a> compiles all merchant source routes/middleware with selected published CMS rows and the source beta2 sandbox, not production configuration or a signed installation. Actual plain/enhanced mug forms, $18 unit/$54 subtotal, Secure/HttpOnly cookie, blank-quantity preservation, foreign-origin/browser isolation, restart-persistent 429 and paused receipt recovery pass; private mounts hide operational files and no Payments/hosted consents are copied. Eight driver guards, thirteen candidate tests and twelve painted audits pass (<a href="/pr-proof/merchant-storefront-https/cart-desktop-light.jpg">cart</a> / <a href="/pr-proof/merchant-storefront-https/checkout-mobile-dark.jpg">checkout</a>), while all seven own PRs still await review and stable remains 0.8.0.</p>
<p class="small" data-installed-retained-review>Original saved-state recovery · <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/commit/88bf394">preparation 88bf394</a> passes eight actual browser journeys for TEST1009/1010 over local canonical HTTPS, using the compiled sandbox and real receipt page/wrapper with selected merchant rows/media but no Payments, users, settings or hosted consents. Frozen identity/items/quantities/totals, current fulfillment, actual artwork, print, cross-tab revocation and separate cart cookie pass; original files and copied business rows remain unchanged, with five driver/thirteen candidate tests and a clean four-view redacted audit (<a href="/pr-proof/merchant-retained-runtime/desktop-light.jpg">desktop</a> / <a href="/pr-proof/merchant-retained-runtime/mobile-dark.jpg">phone</a>). This is source-built recovery for two original saved states, not a signed installation, applied upgrade or hosted payment; stable remains 0.8.0 and the seven own PRs still await review.</p>
<p class="small" data-retained-storage-review>Actual merchant storage · <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/commit/8215265">preparation 8215265</a> reads ten original Orders, eleven exact SKUs and the saved TEST1009/1010 capabilities through EmDash’s repository with SQLite write protection, no Payments binding and OS-level network isolation. Frozen receipt facts, current completion, real Regular/Sale pairs and sizes survive; forged/foreign authority and edits to paid carts are refused, with five driver and thirteen candidate tests passing. This is source read compatibility, not installed-artifact migration or original-browser rendering. All seven own upstream PRs were rechecked November 16 at 03:22 UTC: no new actionable review or code failure; the live store remains on stable 0.8.0.</p>
<p class="small" data-public-catalog-cart-review>Public catalog cart check · <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/commit/b599c9f">merchant preparation b599c9f</a> passes source-kernel admission and synthetic checkout for all seven families/eleven members, using an anonymous snapshot of current effective prices, stock and size choices. Tee XL is refused; Fleece XL and Tote backorders succeed, with frozen-cart and invalid-choice checks plus fourteen driver and thirteen candidate cart tests passing. Four omitted child SKUs use explicit fixture aliases; this is not storage migration, signed Registry/browser or hosted payment qualification. Stable remains 0.8.0; no live purchase or upstream submission was made.</p>
